# Quark Monorepo — Contributor Rules

> For app developers building WITH Quark: see `CLAUDE.md` in your scaffolded project.
> For the full contributor reference: see `CLAUDE.md` at the monorepo root.

---

## Non-Negotiable Rules

1. **ESM only.** Always `import`/`export`. Never `require()` or `module.exports`.
2. **No TypeScript.** Plain `.js` and `.jsx` files only — no `.ts`, `.tsx`, or type annotations.
3. **Biome for everything.** No ESLint, no Prettier. Run `pnpm lint` to check.
4. **Validate at boundaries.** Zod schemas on all Server Actions and API routes. No exceptions.
5. **Use AppError — not Error.** Throw `AppError` / `ValidationError` from `@techstream/quark-core/errors`. Never `throw new Error()` in application code.
6. **Log — never console.** `createLogger(name)` from `@techstream/quark-core`. Zero `console.log` / `console.error` in non-test code.
7. **DB models always have timestamps.** Every Prisma model: `createdAt DateTime @default(now())` + `updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt`.
8. **Co-located tests.** `feature.test.js` next to `feature.js`. `node --test` — no Jest, no Vitest.

---

## Published vs Scaffolded

| Package | Distributed as | Import path |
|---|---|---|
| `packages/core` | Published to npm | `@techstream/quark-core` |
| `packages/cli` | Published to npm | `@techstream/quark-create-app` |
| `packages/db`, `config`, `ui`, `jobs` | Scaffolded locally | `@<scope>/db` etc. in user projects |

Never add `packages/db`, `config`, `ui`, or `jobs` as dependencies of `quark-core` or `quark-create-app`. They are scaffolded into user projects — not published.

---

## Template Sync (CRITICAL)

`packages/cli/templates/` is **generated from monorepo source** — never edit it manually (except `TEMPLATE_ONLY` files like `CLAUDE.md`, `.cursor/rules/quark.mdc`, `SKILL.md`, and workflow files).

After changing any file in `apps/web/`, `apps/worker/`, `packages/db/`, `packages/config/`, `packages/ui/`, or `packages/jobs/`:

```bash
pnpm --filter @techstream/quark-create-app sync-templates
```

CI fails if templates are stale. Always sync before committing.

---

## Release Workflow

```bash
pnpm changeset        # Create a changeset (interactive) — do this after your changes
# Never run: pnpm changeset version   ← CI handles this automatically
```

Only `@techstream/quark-core` and `@techstream/quark-create-app` are versioned and published. All scaffolded packages are excluded from changesets.

---

## Commands

```bash
pnpm dev                          # Start web + worker
pnpm test                         # Run all tests (requires Docker: postgres + redis)
pnpm lint                         # Biome lint + format check
pnpm build                        # Build all packages
pnpm db:generate                  # Regenerate Prisma client
pnpm db:migrate                   # Apply migrations
pnpm --filter <pkg> <script>      # Run script in a specific package
pnpm --filter @techstream/quark-create-app sync-templates        # Sync templates
pnpm --filter @techstream/quark-create-app sync-templates:check  # Check for drift
```

---

## Testing

Requires Postgres 16 + Redis 7. Start both with `docker compose up -d` before running `pnpm test`.

Test utilities and model factories: `packages/core/src/testing/`.
